":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsynchronousUnitOfWork\/Success","text":"Success","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent22AsynchronousUnitOfWorkP7SuccessQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Clock","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP"},{"kind":"text","text":"\n"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The duration to delay the output, conforming to the clock’s associated "},{"code":"Duration","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" type."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"duration"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The clock used for timekeeping."}]}],"name":"clock"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An optional tolerance for the delay. Defaults to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"name":"tolerance"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"How the delay is randomized. Defaults to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BackoffJitter\/none","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Decorrelated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"jitter waits at most three times ","type":"text"},{"code":"duration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"jitter"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsynchronousUnitOfWork"},{"type":"text","text":" that emits the upstream output after the specified delay."}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This operator suspends the emission of output for the specified duration according to the provided clock."}]},{"anchor":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Delaying work using a custom clock is beneficial when you need precise control over timing behavior,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such as testing with test clocks or synchronizing work with specific time sources."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Use this operator to implement retry backoff, throttling, or scheduled tasks that depend on a particular clock implementation."}]},{"anchor":"Example","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Example"},{"code":["let start = Date()","let clock = SuspendingClock()","let delayedTask = DeferredTask {","    \"Delayed with custom clock\"","}.delay(for: .seconds(1), clock: clock, tolerance: .milliseconds(100))","let result = try await delayedTask.execute()","let elapsed = Date().timeIntervalSince(start)","print(\"Result: \\(result) after \\(elapsed) seconds\")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Availability: macOS 13.0, iOS 16.0, watchOS 9.0, tvOS 16.0, visionOS 1.0 and above.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On WASI, a sleep on a real clock (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ContinuousClock"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SuspendingClock"},{"text":") holds the one thread","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until its deadline, even when other work is ready, and cancelling it doesn’t end it sooner. So the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delay always waits out its whole duration, even when cancelled. A test clock is unaffected.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Note"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","s